  "_comment": "Plan 19a: what scripts/differential-windows.ps1 checks. Nothing here deletes or changes anything: PowerShell lines are only parsed, never run. cmd lines run in a throwaway directory and call only `echo`, `type` of a scratch file, `cd`, and p19adiffstub, a batch file that logs its arguments. `over` and `powershell_over` mark a documented over-read: the reader sees a command the shell does not run, which is a false deny and not a bypass. A string in `over` is why that is safe. `powershell_documented` pins a line the reader reads differently from the parser, both readings exact, so any other mismatch still fails; `powershell_report` is only printed. `alias_only_51` are aliases in Windows PowerShell 5.1 and real programs in 7; `alias_over` are aliases the reader over-reads, with why.",
