      "over_reader": "c:/windows",
      "over": "Git Bash does not mount /cygdrive by default, so cygpath puts it under the install folder of Git (C:\\Program Files\\Git\\cygdrive\\c\\Windows). The reader says c:/Windows, which can at most deny a delete of a harmless folder there and never allows one of the real Windows folder: the safe direction. Accepted only while cygpath's answer ends in the raw path (unmounted) and the reader says exactly over_reader; a mounted /cygdrive that disagrees still fails."
